  "summary": "Unlike Aero , the design language of the time never had a formal designation as it was literally developing with each implementations and technological innovations—no formal design took place in Windows until Windows 95.",
  "description": "Unlike Aero , the design language of the time never had a formal designation as it was literally developing with each implementations and technological innovations—no formal design took place in Windows until Windows 95. The name is thus taken from the fact that pixels were often the basic unit of these designs because individual pixels were still easily distinguished on display technologies of the time.",
